{
 "title": "Automatic cleanup and defer",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Greengold has no garbage collector. When a Move type reaches the end of the scope it was defined in, the compiler frees the memory **by itself** (`drop`). You never write `free` and you cannot forget it."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "**`defer`** marks cleanup code to run when a scope is left (a normal exit, `return`, `break`, `continue`, an error: all the same). Several `defer`s run in **reverse order** (the last written runs first)."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "fn main():",
    "    print(\"started\")",
    "    defer print(\"cleanup 1 (written first, runs last)\")",
    "    defer print(\"cleanup 2\")",
    "    defer print(\"cleanup 3 (written last, runs first)\")",
    "    print(\"working...\")"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "started",
    "working...",
    "cleanup 3 (written last, runs first)",
    "cleanup 2",
    "cleanup 1 (written first, runs last)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "fn process(code: i32):",
    "    print(\"resource opened\")",
    "    defer print(\"resource closed\")",
    "    if code < 0:",
    "        print(\"error, returning early\")",
    "        return",
    "    print(\"processed\")",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    process(1)",
    "    process(-1)"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "resource opened",
    "processed",
    "resource closed",
    "resource opened",
    "error, returning early",
    "resource closed"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "exercise",
   "id": "c05-l06-x1",
   "prompt": "In `run()` print the messages `open`, `use` and `close`; but write `close` with `defer`, right after `open`. The expected order is: open, use, close.",
   "starter": [
    "fn run():",
    "    print(\"open\")",
    "    print(\"use\")",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    run()"
   ],
   "solution": [
    "fn run():",
    "    print(\"open\")",
    "    defer print(\"close\")",
    "    print(\"use\")",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    run()"
   ],
   "hint": "Add `defer print(\"close\")` below `print(\"open\")`.",
   "expected": [
    "open",
    "use",
    "close"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "quiz",
   "id": "c05-l06-q1",
   "q": "With three `defer`s written, which runs first?",
   "options": [
    "The first written",
    "The last written",
    "A random one"
   ],
   "answer": 1,
   "why": "`defer`s run in reverse order (LIFO)."
  }
 ]
}
